; The mgtt bridge: an mgtt model read as a writ model.
;
; It lives in tooling/ for the reason tooling/sql/ does, and the reason is worth
; restating rather than inferred. `core/` is the LANGUAGE — the data model, the
; front end, the standard library. Everything that bridges writ to something
; foreign lives here: `json` and `loadpath`, `lsp` and `mcp`, `sql`. An mgtt
; export reader is a bridge to a foreign NOTATION exactly as writ_lsp is a
; bridge to a foreign PROTOCOL, and putting one beside writ_data would assert
; that mgtt is part of what writ IS. It is not; the engine cannot tell this
; library exists.
;
; Flat rather than lib/ + bin/, which is `json`'s and `sql`'s shape and not
; `lsp`'s: those split because they produce their own executable. `writ mgtt`
; is a verb of the one CLI, so there is no second binary to separate from.
;
; It depends on [writ_json] to read the export document and NOTHING ELSE — not
; the data model, not the front end, not the interrogator. That is not an
; accident of what it happens to need: the output is .writ TEXT, so a malformed
; export can never reach the engine, and the whole mapping stays testable
; without a filesystem or a parser.
;
; IO-free, like every library here; the `writ mgtt` verb in tooling/cli/ does
; the reading and the writing.

(library
 (name writ_mgtt)
 (libraries writ_json))
